1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,916
Your tests pass. Two out of two. Green. So, is the shop safe to ship?

2
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:05,955
Not yet.

3
00:00:05,955 --> 00:00:10,116
Because a green test only tells you that the lines it ran were fine.

4
00:00:10,116 --> 00:00:12,869
It says nothing about the lines it never ran.

5
00:00:13,419 --> 00:00:15,653
Test coverage answers one question.

6
00:00:15,653 --> 00:00:18,653
How much of my code did the tests actually run?

7
00:00:18,653 --> 00:00:21,525
And it shows you the lines nobody has tested.

8
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:25,669
Today you measure coverage on the CloudCart pricing code,

9
00:00:25,669 --> 00:00:26,784
with pytest-cov.

10
00:00:26,784 --> 00:00:28,334
You open the real report.

11
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:33,105
And you learn the big limit: a hundred percent coverage can still miss a bug.

12
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:36,084
Here is what to expect.

13
00:00:36,634 --> 00:00:39,600
One: what coverage measures. Lines, and branches.

14
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:43,222
Two: how to run it, and read the report, in the terminal.

15
00:00:43,772 --> 00:00:47,782
Three: the limits. Why high coverage is not the same as good tests.

16
00:00:48,332 --> 00:00:49,476
Then a live demo.

17
00:00:49,476 --> 00:00:51,561
We start at forty-five percent,

18
00:00:51,561 --> 00:00:54,386
open the real HTML report in a browser,

19
00:00:54,386 --> 00:00:55,933
and climb to a hundred.

20
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:57,278
Then we plant a bug,

21
00:00:57,278 --> 00:00:58,892
and see it slip through.

22
00:00:59,442 --> 00:01:04,221
And a lab with six checks, including one that plants four bugs, to test your tests.

23
00:01:06,271 --> 00:01:07,722
What does coverage measure?

24
00:01:08,272 --> 00:01:09,596
While your tests run,

25
00:01:09,596 --> 00:01:11,109
a tool watches the code.

26
00:01:11,109 --> 00:01:13,190
Every line that runs gets a tick.

27
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:13,884
At the end,

28
00:01:13,884 --> 00:01:15,713
it tells you which lines ran,

29
00:01:15,713 --> 00:01:16,848
and which did not.

30
00:01:17,398 --> 00:01:22,496
That is statement coverage. Twenty-one statements, twelve ran, nine did not. Simple.

31
00:01:23,046 --> 00:01:24,585
Then there are branches.

32
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:26,444
An if has two ways out: true,

33
00:01:26,444 --> 00:01:27,021
or false.

34
00:01:27,021 --> 00:01:29,907
Branch coverage asks if your tests took both.

35
00:01:29,907 --> 00:01:32,215
A test that only ever enters the if,

36
00:01:32,215 --> 00:01:34,972
never checks what happens when it does not.

37
00:01:35,522 --> 00:01:36,200
In Python,

38
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,167
the tool is coverage.py.

39
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:40,879
And pytest-cov plugs it into pytest,

40
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:41,964
with one option.

41
00:01:42,514 --> 00:01:46,145
The point: coverage finds the code your tests never touch.

42
00:01:46,145 --> 00:01:48,210
That is where untested bugs hide.

43
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:50,827
How do you run it?

44
00:01:51,377 --> 00:01:56,177
Add dash dash cov, and the name of the module. That prints a table in the terminal.

45
00:01:56,727 --> 00:01:59,102
Add cov report equals term-missing,

46
00:01:59,102 --> 00:02:01,545
and the table gets a Missing column.

47
00:02:01,545 --> 00:02:03,852
The exact line numbers nobody ran.

48
00:02:04,402 --> 00:02:06,479
Or cov report equals HTML,

49
00:02:06,479 --> 00:02:08,698
to write a folder of web pages.

50
00:02:08,698 --> 00:02:09,772
Open the index,

51
00:02:09,772 --> 00:02:12,637
and click a file: every line is colored.

52
00:02:13,187 --> 00:02:14,444
And --cov-fail-under,

53
00:02:14,444 --> 00:02:15,371
with a number.

54
00:02:15,371 --> 00:02:17,159
If coverage drops below it,

55
00:02:17,159 --> 00:02:18,086
the run fails,

56
00:02:18,086 --> 00:02:19,741
and so does the pipeline.

57
00:02:19,741 --> 00:02:20,204
A gate,

58
00:02:20,204 --> 00:02:21,528
for the next lesson.

59
00:02:22,078 --> 00:02:27,774
Switch on branch coverage in a small file, .coveragerc, so you see partial lines too.

60
00:02:29,324 --> 00:02:32,503
Now the part most people miss. The limits of coverage.

61
00:02:33,053 --> 00:02:34,965
Coverage counts lines that ran.

62
00:02:34,965 --> 00:02:36,692
Not lines that were checked.

63
00:02:36,692 --> 00:02:38,049
A test with no assert,

64
00:02:38,049 --> 00:02:40,454
can run a hundred percent of your code,

65
00:02:40,454 --> 00:02:41,565
and prove nothing.

66
00:02:42,115 --> 00:02:44,033
Look for the bug that survives.

67
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:46,137
Plant a small mistake in the code,

68
00:02:46,137 --> 00:02:47,127
a wrong divisor,

69
00:02:47,127 --> 00:02:48,179
a wrong boundary.

70
00:02:48,179 --> 00:02:49,726
If your tests still pass,

71
00:02:49,726 --> 00:02:51,459
they are not protecting you.

72
00:02:52,009 --> 00:02:54,073
Boundaries are the classic miss.

73
00:02:54,073 --> 00:02:55,428
Seventy-five hundred,

74
00:02:55,428 --> 00:02:57,299
and seventy-four ninety-nine.

75
00:02:57,299 --> 00:02:58,331
Twenty thousand,

76
00:02:58,331 --> 00:03:01,363
and nineteen thousand nine hundred ninety-nine.

77
00:03:01,363 --> 00:03:02,718
Test the exact edges.

78
00:03:03,268 --> 00:03:06,534
So use coverage the right way: to find what you forgot,

79
00:03:06,534 --> 00:03:08,078
not to prove you are done.

80
00:03:08,078 --> 00:03:09,800
Chasing the number is a trap.

81
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,691
Ninety percent,

82
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:11,879
with strong asserts,

83
00:03:11,879 --> 00:03:13,423
beats a hundred with none.

84
00:03:13,973 --> 00:03:16,597
And remember, covered code is not correct code.

85
00:03:18,147 --> 00:03:22,947
Go to the lab folder.

86
00:03:24,497 --> 00:03:26,396
Look around.

87
00:03:26,946 --> 00:03:27,722
Our module,

88
00:03:27,722 --> 00:03:28,640
cart.py,

89
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,687
the CloudCart pricing rules.

90
00:03:30,687 --> 00:03:32,805
A tests folder with two tests.

91
00:03:32,805 --> 00:03:34,075
And an out folder,

92
00:03:34,075 --> 00:03:34,499
empty,

93
00:03:34,499 --> 00:03:35,628
for our reports.

94
00:03:36,178 --> 00:03:39,976
Run the tests.

95
00:03:40,526 --> 00:03:44,664
Two passed. All green. But how much of cart.py did they run?

96
00:03:45,214 --> 00:03:49,801
Measure it.

97
00:03:50,351 --> 00:03:51,171
A new table.

98
00:03:51,171 --> 00:03:52,674
Twenty-one statements,

99
00:03:52,674 --> 00:03:53,494
nine missed.

100
00:03:53,494 --> 00:03:54,588
Twelve branches,

101
00:03:54,588 --> 00:03:56,775
three of them only partly taken.

102
00:03:56,775 --> 00:03:58,756
Coverage: forty-five percent.

103
00:03:59,306 --> 00:04:04,042
Which lines?

104
00:04:06,592 --> 00:04:07,781
The Missing column.

105
00:04:07,781 --> 00:04:08,469
Lines five,

106
00:04:08,469 --> 00:04:08,844
eight,

107
00:04:08,844 --> 00:04:10,408
and thirteen to nineteen.

108
00:04:10,408 --> 00:04:12,848
That is the shipping for an empty cart,

109
00:04:12,848 --> 00:04:14,599
the standard shipping price,

110
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:16,476
and all of the discount codes.

111
00:04:16,476 --> 00:04:17,664
Nobody tested them.

112
00:04:17,664 --> 00:04:18,853
This file is saved,

113
00:04:18,853 --> 00:04:20,416
and the lab will read it.

114
00:04:20,966 --> 00:04:29,457
An HTML report.

115
00:04:30,007 --> 00:04:34,594
Coverage HTML written. A folder of web pages. Let us open it.

116
00:04:35,144 --> 00:04:36,166
Numbers are good.

117
00:04:36,166 --> 00:04:37,248
Colors are better.

118
00:04:37,248 --> 00:04:39,412
Let us open the report in a browser,

119
00:04:39,412 --> 00:04:41,096
and look at the code itself.

120
00:04:41,646 --> 00:04:42,767
I open Chrome,

121
00:04:42,767 --> 00:04:45,572
and type the path to the file: out,

122
00:04:45,572 --> 00:04:46,533
htmlcov,

123
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:47,975
index.html.

124
00:04:47,975 --> 00:04:48,456
Again,

125
00:04:48,456 --> 00:04:49,818
no server needed.

126
00:04:49,818 --> 00:04:52,142
It is just a folder of files.

127
00:04:52,692 --> 00:04:53,862
This is the index.

128
00:04:53,862 --> 00:04:55,941
The title says: coverage report,

129
00:04:55,941 --> 00:04:57,176
forty-five percent.

130
00:04:57,176 --> 00:04:57,566
Below,

131
00:04:57,566 --> 00:04:58,086
a table,

132
00:04:58,086 --> 00:04:59,581
one row for every file.

133
00:04:59,581 --> 00:05:00,426
cart.py.

134
00:05:00,426 --> 00:05:01,921
Statements: twenty-one,

135
00:05:01,921 --> 00:05:02,766
nine missing,

136
00:05:02,766 --> 00:05:03,676
none excluded.

137
00:05:03,676 --> 00:05:05,366
Then the branches: twelve,

138
00:05:05,366 --> 00:05:06,601
with three partial.

139
00:05:06,601 --> 00:05:08,096
And the total coverage,

140
00:05:08,096 --> 00:05:08,941
on the right.

141
00:05:08,941 --> 00:05:10,046
In a big project,

142
00:05:10,046 --> 00:05:11,541
this table is your map.

143
00:05:11,541 --> 00:05:13,945
You click the column headers to sort,

144
00:05:13,945 --> 00:05:16,350
and find the least tested file first.

145
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,381
I click the file name,

146
00:05:18,381 --> 00:05:19,997
and now we see the code.

147
00:05:19,997 --> 00:05:22,286
At the top: twenty-one statements.

148
00:05:22,286 --> 00:05:23,027
Twelve run.

149
00:05:23,027 --> 00:05:23,902
Nine missing.

150
00:05:23,902 --> 00:05:24,844
Three partial.

151
00:05:24,844 --> 00:05:26,932
Those four buttons are filters.

152
00:05:26,932 --> 00:05:30,298
And the colors are on the left edge of every line.

153
00:05:30,848 --> 00:05:31,935
Green lines ran.

154
00:05:31,935 --> 00:05:33,294
Red lines never ran.

155
00:05:33,294 --> 00:05:34,721
Look at the red ones.

156
00:05:34,721 --> 00:05:35,400
Line five,

157
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,419
the empty cart.

158
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:37,167
Line eight,

159
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:39,069
the standard shipping price.

160
00:05:39,069 --> 00:05:42,602
And lines thirteen to nineteen: every discount code.

161
00:05:43,152 --> 00:05:44,757
I click the missing button,

162
00:05:44,757 --> 00:05:46,362
and the red lines light up.

163
00:05:46,362 --> 00:05:47,729
Only the problem lines,

164
00:05:47,729 --> 00:05:48,442
highlighted.

165
00:05:48,442 --> 00:05:49,869
That is your to do list.

166
00:05:49,869 --> 00:05:52,603
Every red line is a test you have not written.

167
00:05:53,153 --> 00:05:54,745
And now the yellow ones.

168
00:05:54,745 --> 00:05:56,935
Look at line four: the note says,

169
00:05:56,935 --> 00:05:57,267
four,

170
00:05:57,267 --> 00:05:57,665
arrow,

171
00:05:57,665 --> 00:05:57,997
five.

172
00:05:57,997 --> 00:06:00,916
The test jumped to line five from line four,

173
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:02,840
but never took the other way.

174
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,499
That is a partial branch.

175
00:06:04,499 --> 00:06:05,627
Same on line six,

176
00:06:05,627 --> 00:06:06,689
and line eleven.

177
00:06:06,689 --> 00:06:07,551
The code ran,

178
00:06:07,551 --> 00:06:09,409
but only one side of the if.

179
00:06:24,859 --> 00:06:25,379
Press R,

180
00:06:25,379 --> 00:06:27,591
and the run lines are highlighted.

181
00:06:27,591 --> 00:06:28,112
Press M,

182
00:06:28,112 --> 00:06:28,893
and missing.

183
00:06:28,893 --> 00:06:29,413
Press P,

184
00:06:29,413 --> 00:06:30,194
for partial.

185
00:06:30,194 --> 00:06:32,080
Those are keyboard shortcuts,

186
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:34,032
you can see the keyboard icon,

187
00:06:34,032 --> 00:06:34,683
top right,

188
00:06:34,683 --> 00:06:35,854
for the full list.

189
00:06:35,854 --> 00:06:37,480
Press the same key again,

190
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,302
and the highlight goes away.

191
00:06:39,852 --> 00:06:40,530
To go back,

192
00:06:40,530 --> 00:06:41,271
click index.

193
00:06:41,271 --> 00:06:42,381
Back to the table,

194
00:06:42,381 --> 00:06:43,616
with the percentage.

195
00:06:43,616 --> 00:06:46,454
This is the page you attach to a pull request,

196
00:06:46,454 --> 00:06:47,873
or keep with the build.

197
00:06:48,423 --> 00:06:53,799
That is the report. Now we go back to the terminal, and fix the red lines, one at a time.

198
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:18,097
Test one: edges.

199
00:07:25,547 --> 00:07:26,307
Two asserts.

200
00:07:26,307 --> 00:07:28,779
Seventy-four ninety-nine pays shipping,

201
00:07:28,779 --> 00:07:30,617
and an empty cart ships free.

202
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:34,166
Those are the edges around the red lines five and eight.

203
00:07:34,716 --> 00:07:40,134
Measure again.

204
00:07:41,184 --> 00:07:42,393
Fifty-eight percent.

205
00:07:42,393 --> 00:07:44,992
Lines five and eight are gone from Missing.

206
00:07:44,992 --> 00:07:46,987
Only thirteen to nineteen remain.

207
00:07:47,537 --> 00:07:51,974
Test two: codes.

208
00:08:06,024 --> 00:08:06,803
Welcome ten.

209
00:08:06,803 --> 00:08:07,388
And bulk,

210
00:08:07,388 --> 00:08:09,141
at exactly twenty thousand,

211
00:08:09,141 --> 00:08:12,387
and at nineteen thousand nine hundred ninety-nine,

212
00:08:12,387 --> 00:08:13,685
just below the edge.

213
00:08:13,685 --> 00:08:14,464
Real totals,

214
00:08:14,464 --> 00:08:15,048
in cents.

215
00:08:15,598 --> 00:08:17,390
Measure again.

216
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:26,968
Ninety-four percent. One line left: nineteen. The error for an unknown code.

217
00:08:27,518 --> 00:08:33,940
Test three: error.

218
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:42,931
An unknown code must be refused.

219
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:45,273
Measure again.

220
00:08:49,923 --> 00:08:53,486
A hundred percent. Nothing missing, and no partial branches.

221
00:08:54,036 --> 00:08:58,388
A gate.

222
00:08:59,638 --> 00:09:02,800
Required test coverage of ninety percent reached.

223
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,349
If it had dropped below,

224
00:09:04,349 --> 00:09:05,640
this run would fail.

225
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:09,835
That is how a pipeline refuses a pull request that removes tests.

226
00:09:10,385 --> 00:09:18,129
A hollow test.

227
00:09:33,679 --> 00:09:34,984
It calls total cents,

228
00:09:34,984 --> 00:09:35,978
with every code,

229
00:09:35,978 --> 00:09:36,909
and every size.

230
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:39,332
And look: there is not a single assert.

231
00:09:39,882 --> 00:09:43,018
Measure it.

232
00:09:46,768 --> 00:09:47,333
One test.

233
00:09:47,333 --> 00:09:48,022
No asserts.

234
00:09:48,022 --> 00:09:49,716
A hundred percent coverage.

235
00:09:49,716 --> 00:09:51,221
The number says perfect,

236
00:09:51,221 --> 00:09:52,976
and the test proves nothing.

237
00:09:53,526 --> 00:09:58,774
Save the file.

238
00:09:59,324 --> 00:10:08,562
Plant the bug.

239
00:10:09,112 --> 00:10:14,018
See it.

240
00:10:14,568 --> 00:10:18,280
Line fourteen. Welcome ten now gives one percent, not ten.

241
00:10:18,830 --> 00:10:22,820
The hollow test.

242
00:10:23,370 --> 00:10:28,298
Passed. A hundred percent coverage, and the bug walked right through. Nobody noticed.

243
00:10:28,848 --> 00:10:32,986
The real tests.

244
00:10:33,536 --> 00:10:33,974
Failed.

245
00:10:33,974 --> 00:10:36,910
The summary names the test: the discount codes.

246
00:10:36,910 --> 00:10:38,534
The assert caught the bug.

247
00:10:38,534 --> 00:10:39,409
Same coverage,

248
00:10:39,409 --> 00:10:41,408
completely different protection.

249
00:10:41,958 --> 00:10:46,822
Restore it.

250
00:10:47,372 --> 00:10:51,063
All green.

251
00:10:51,613 --> 00:10:53,576
Six passed. The bug is gone.

252
00:10:54,126 --> 00:11:00,206
Where am I?

253
00:11:00,756 --> 00:11:01,789
Four out of six.

254
00:11:01,789 --> 00:11:02,370
Coverage,

255
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,080
the report,

256
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,564
and the bug check pass.

257
00:11:04,564 --> 00:11:07,405
I still need a sixth test with real asserts,

258
00:11:07,405 --> 00:11:08,696
and my final report.

259
00:11:08,696 --> 00:11:10,697
That is the start of your task.

260
00:11:11,247 --> 00:11:13,210
Clean up.

261
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,616
Removed. Nothing left behind.

262
00:11:17,166 --> 00:11:21,910
Your lab task: take the coverage from forty-five percent to ninety or more,

263
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:23,745
with tests that really check.

264
00:11:23,745 --> 00:11:24,441
Six checks.

265
00:11:24,991 --> 00:11:29,983
One: save the start report. Two: make the HTML report, and open it.

266
00:11:30,533 --> 00:11:36,357
Three: add tests until cart.py reaches ninety percent. You may not edit cart.py.

267
00:11:36,907 --> 00:11:40,704
Four: write six tests or more, and every one must assert something.

268
00:11:41,254 --> 00:11:43,555
Five: lab check plants four bugs,

269
00:11:43,555 --> 00:11:44,321
one by one,

270
00:11:44,321 --> 00:11:45,716
and runs your tests.

271
00:11:45,716 --> 00:11:48,156
At least three bugs must be caught.

272
00:11:48,156 --> 00:11:49,619
Test the exact edges.

273
00:11:49,619 --> 00:11:51,502
Six: save the final report,

274
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:52,547
then lab check,

275
00:11:52,547 --> 00:11:54,011
until six out of six.

276
00:11:56,061 --> 00:11:58,856
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

277
00:11:59,406 --> 00:12:00,870
One: the repository,

278
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:05,190
github.com/it-waves/devops-ai,

279
00:12:05,190 --> 00:12:07,534
in the folder academy/lab.

280
00:12:08,084 --> 00:12:13,481
Two: the files, lab140.sh, and shortcuts140.sh.

281
00:12:14,031 --> 00:12:19,492
Three: install it, with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin/.

282
00:12:20,042 --> 00:12:21,900
Four: load the short names,

283
